      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nope.  When we\u0027re a sink, we can only probe SOP\u0027 from an explicit contract when the Vconn source, which means we start any probing from PE_SNK_READY.  We could miss an incoming SOP\u0027 message from the cable, but since all cable AMSes are written with the cable as a responder there\u0027s no current spec case where we\u0027d expect the cable to just talk to us without us having initiated the AMS from READY.  \n\nIf we\u0027re both the source and Vconn source, we can probe outside the explicit contract from PE_SRC_Discovery.",
